TBD -- "Tiny By Design"
=======================

  TBD is a build system framework intended to support repeated
testing of experimental systems.

 Typical such systems might involve separately-built components,
such as the toolchain, kernel, initrd, and rootfs parts of an OS.
Here, the system, its components, and their build method and build
order are user-definable, as is any system-level configuration they
share.

  Sample systems include linux-style chroot jails which provide
shells built against the musl C library, generated by a suitable
toolchain. These build by providing the top level configuration
directory and invoking either the 'all' target or a rule in the
form 'all-COMPONENT', eg.:
	make CONFIG_DIR=config/qdmusl-chroot1/ all
